{"acceptance_length": 2.801980198019802, "acceptance_lengths": [1, 6, 1, 2, 2, 1, 3, 2, 2, 1, 3, 2, 4, 2, 2, 16, 2, 13, 4, 2, 1, 3, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 1, 3, 5, 1, 3, 6, 1, 1, 1, 3, 4, 2, 1, 1, 2, 4, 4, 4, 1, 5, 4, 1, 1, 1, 10, 7, 4, 1, 2, 1, 6, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 6, 6, 6, 1, 1, 3, 6, 1, 3, 2, 6, 1, 1, 2, 2, 4, 1, 6, 1, 1, 3, 1, 1, 3, 4, 1, 4, 1, 2, 1, 4, 2, 3, 5, 1, 4, 1], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 34409766912, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 34409763840, "benchmark": "math500", "completion": "To solve this problem, we need to use the relationship between interior and exterior angles of a polygon.\n\nLet's denote the measure of an exterior angle as x. Since the measure of an interior angle is 6.5 times the measure of an exterior angle, the measure of an interior angle is 6.5x.\n\nWe know that the sum of an interior angle and its corresponding exterior angle is always 180 degrees. \n\nSo, we can write the equation: \n6.5x + x = 180\n\nCombine like terms:\n7.5x = 180\n\nNow, divide both sides by 7.5:\nx = 180 / 7.5\nx = 24\n\nNow that we know the measure of an exterior angle, we can find the number of sides of the polygon. The sum of all exterior angles of a polygon is always 360 degrees. \n\nLet's denote the number of sides as n. Then, the sum of all exterior angles is nx.\n\nSince the sum of all exterior angles is 360 degrees, we can write the equation:\nnx = 360\n\nNow, substitute the value of x (24) into the equation:\nn(24) = 360\n\nNow, divide both sides by 24:\nn = 360 / 24\nn = 15\n\nTherefore, the polygon has 15 sides.\n\n\\boxed{15}", "decode_seconds": 6.080813473090529, "draft_calls": 101, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 82, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "7ad23f549833b34cbe25e588ccd8cb6980306e33defce755cddb56206030da50", "method": "relay_candidate_1", "output_hash": "b4b8fb5f2cf9efa1fc9dc43bad5cbbeed2f27b1d803b3fe355bf8eabb4bab880", "output_token_ids": [1271, 11886, 420, 3575, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1005, 279, 5133, 1990, 15135, 323, 28362, 27030, 31